WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.996
The software stack begins with an operating-system image.

00:00:03.996 --> 00:00:10.516
Provider images may include GPU drivers and acceleration libraries, while general images require installation.

00:00:10.516 --> 00:00:15.774
Match the NVIDIA driver, CUDA runtime, framework, and GPU architecture deliberately.

00:00:15.774 --> 00:00:26.500
A command that detects the GPU is only the first test; confirm that the chosen framework can allocate memory and execute a representative operation.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:35.964
Containers package applications and dependencies into repeatable units, but they still rely on a compatible host driver and GPU container runtime.

00:00:35.964 --> 00:00:42.063
Pin image versions or immutable digests instead of pulling an uncontrolled latest tag.

00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:47.321
For non-container workflows, create isolated Python environments and record package versions.

00:00:47.321 --> 00:00:56.785
Notebooks are useful for exploration, but a long-lived notebook with manual changes is difficult to reproduce and easy to expose accidentally.

00:00:56.785 --> 00:01:04.567
Model servers turn the instance into a service, and local API endpoints let applications communicate with them.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:11.507
Bind development services to a private interface or loopback address until access controls are ready.

00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:16.765
Document model versions, startup arguments, ports, context settings, and health checks.

00:01:16.765 --> 00:01:27.912
If a web notebook or model interface must be reached remotely, prefer an authenticated private access path over opening a management port to the internet.

00:01:27.912 --> 00:01:32.328
Automate setup with reviewed scripts, images, or infrastructure definitions.

00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:39.269
The goal is to replace a failed or temporary instance without reconstructing it from memory.

00:01:39.269 --> 00:01:43.265
Keep secrets and private data outside reusable images.

00:01:43.265 --> 00:01:51.888
Test the build on a fresh instance, measure provisioning time, and preserve only the components necessary for the workload.

00:01:51.888 --> 00:01:57.987
Reproducibility reduces both operational risk and the billable time spent repairing one-off environments.
